        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "πάντα δέ σοι ἐγὼ δηλώσω, ὅσα ἐάν σοι δείξω. ἔμβλεπε οὖν τοῖς λοιποῖς.",
          "english_quote": "Retain the gate/rock relationship, shared load-bearing, condition on understanding and the tower lord’s inspection.",
          "issue": "The unit's theological metadata attributes a tower lord’s inspection to this selected passage, which contains no tower or inspection. Its accompanying rationale also refers to disputed counts and conjectural negation that belong to other units, not this one. This inaccurately describes the source choices documented for S.9.ii.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restrict this unit's metadata to its actual scene and decisions, including the rock, gate, virgins, and the shepherd's instruction concerning understanding. Move inspection, disputed stone counts, and conjectural-negation documentation to the applicable units. Review the revised metadata before acceptance.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "οὕτως ἕτοιμοι ἦσαν· λίαν γὰρ ἱλαραὶ ἦσαν καὶ πρόθυμοι.",
          "english_quote": "They were ready, cheerful and eager.",
          "issue": "The simplified text drops the explicit degree expressed by λίαν. Unlike the standard's “very cheerful,” it no longer preserves the source-backed emphasis.",
          "suggested_revision": "A candidate for fresh review is: “They were ready like this, for they were very cheerful and eager.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἀλλ᾿ ἐρώτα τὸν Κύριον, ἵνα λάβῃς σύνεσιν νοεῖν αὐτά.",
          "english_quote": "Ask the Lord to give you understanding.",
          "issue": "The request for understanding remains, but the explicit purpose and object—understanding those things that Hermas cannot comprehend—are omitted. The source does not merely direct him to ask for understanding in general.",
          "suggested_revision": "A candidate for fresh review is: “Instead, ask the Lord to give you understanding so that you can understand those things.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τὰ ὀπίσω σου ἰδεῖν οὐ δύνῃ, τὰ δὲ ἔμπροσθέν σου βλέπεις. ἃ οὖν ἰδεῖν οὐ δύνασαι, ἔασον, καὶ μὴ στρέβλου σεαυτόν· ἃ δὲ βλέπεις, ἐκείνων κατακυρίευε",
          "english_quote": "You cannot see behind you, but you can see what is in front of you. Leave what you cannot see alone. Do not torment yourself. Master what you can see",
          "issue": "The source contrasts inability to see what is behind with actual sight of what is before Hermas, and then commands mastery of what he actually sees. Twice substituting “can see” for βλέπεις changes actual perception into potential visibility and broadens the command's object.",
          "suggested_revision": "Candidates for fresh review are: “You cannot see behind you, but you see what is in front of you” and “Master what you see.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "πάντα δέ σοι ἐγὼ δηλώσω, ὅσα ἐάν σοι δείξω. ἔμβλεπε οὖν τοῖς λοιποῖς.",
          "english_quote": "Retain the gate/rock relationship, shared load-bearing, condition on understanding and the tower lord’s inspection.",
          "issue": "As in the standard edition, this theological metadata attributes an inspection to a passage containing no tower or inspection. The rationale's disputed counts and conjectural negation likewise do not occur in this selected unit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace the cross-unit description with metadata limited to decisions actually made in S.9.ii, and retain the other matters only in their applicable units. Submit the replacement for fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "κύκλῳ δὲ τῆς πύλης εἱστήκεισαν παρθένοι δώδεκα.",
          "english_quote": "Retain rock/gate distinctions, shared carrying, stone counts, the explicitly conjectural negative and the distinction between a pause and completion; preserve all substantive alternative notes.",
          "issue": "The simplification metadata claims preservation of stone counts, a conjectural negative, and a pause/completion distinction absent from S.9.ii. The selected passage counts virgins, not stones. This is inaccurate unit-specific documentation, not evidence that those source-critical issues were handled here.",
          "suggested_revision": "Document the actual simplifications in this unit and remove or relocate the claims concerning stone counts, conjectural negation, and pause versus completion. Review the replacement independently.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The standard reader text is faithful to the selected working Greek, but its unit-specific metadata needs correction. The simplified text independently requires restoration of explicit emphasis, the stated purpose of understanding, and the distinction between actual sight and ability to see, as well as metadata repair. The bounded witness notes distinguish damaged or supplied material from preserved text and do not claim complete manuscript verification. The disclosed construal of συνετὸς ὤν is not rejected merely because literal alternatives exist. This review does not authenticate unseen editions or manuscript images; proposed revisions require fresh review."
}
